robot-browser (3.6.0-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * A terminal marked "Secure Terminal" on the SCADA server locks itself and
    asks a worker to sign on; switching it back to Open removes the lock within
    seconds, without a restart
  * A worker signs on with one value - keyed, or presented as a card through
    the wsrobot reader bridge
  * Signing on posts publishLogon and shows the server's own wording when it is
    refused; locking, the lock button and shutdown all sign the worker off with
    publishLogoff
  * The lock timeout is in Settings, defaulting to five minutes
  * Fix: a page asking for HTTP credentials could open a dialog over the lock
  * Fix: the on-screen keyboard sent keystrokes to the hidden page while locked
  * Fix: the idle countdown ran from the last touch instead of from the sign-on

 -- Jan Zwiegers <jan@radicalsystems.co.za>  Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200

robot-browser (3.5.0-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Pick a device profile from the Settings dialog; --profile=user applies
    whatever was saved, so the choice survives a restart
  * A device profile reproduces the viewport only - no WiFi indicator, SCADA
    state or on-screen keyboard on a machine that is not a terminal
  * The device and its scale are named in the title bar
  * Menu entry and icon are named io.radsys.RobotBrowser
  * Fix: a saved profile was resolved after the fit-to-screen calculation, so
    it opened at a different size than the same profile named on the command
    line
  * Fix: no window icon was ever set, and the icon file could not be read by
    GTK at all - a comment ahead of <svg pushed it past what gdk-pixbuf sniffs

 -- Jan Zwiegers <jan@radicalsystems.co.za>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200

